1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:05,933
AI coding agents say they fixed your accessibility bugs.

2
00:00:05,583 --> 00:00:07,316
But how do you know?

3
00:00:08,066 --> 00:00:11,320
A11Y Lens is a plugin for Hermes.

4
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:15,418
It opens the page in a real headless Chromium.

5
00:00:15,068 --> 00:00:18,856
And runs the axe-core engine against the rendered DOM.

6
00:00:18,506 --> 00:00:20,750
Thirty-nine violations.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,994
Not guessed.

8
00:00:21,644 --> 00:00:22,936
Measured.

9
00:00:22,586 --> 00:00:28,429
Every finding carries a CSS selector, the HTML, and the reason it fails.

10
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:33,861
Every number in this report is axe-core output from an actual browser run.

11
00:00:33,511 --> 00:00:37,102
An empty button. Images with no alt text.

12
00:00:36,752 --> 00:00:40,947
Contrast eight times too low. A select with no label.

13
00:00:41,697 --> 00:00:44,951
A11Y Lens never edits your code.

14
00:00:44,601 --> 00:00:48,622
The agent repairs the source with its normal file tools.

15
00:00:49,372 --> 00:00:53,427
Adding labels, alt text, lang, a title.

16
00:00:53,077 --> 00:00:55,147
Fixing the role typo.

17
00:00:54,797 --> 00:00:57,273
Real contrast values.

18
00:00:56,923 --> 00:00:59,272
Computed on real colors.

19
00:01:00,022 --> 00:01:02,428
Now, the part that matters.

20
00:01:02,078 --> 00:01:04,938
Re-open the page. Re-test.

21
00:01:05,688 --> 00:01:07,038
Compare.

22
00:01:06,688 --> 00:01:10,291
Resolved. Remaining. And newly introduced.

23
00:01:11,041 --> 00:01:13,923
Regressions the agent cannot hide.

24
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,283
Not "trust me".

25
00:01:16,033 --> 00:01:18,057
The rendered page.

26
00:01:17,707 --> 00:01:19,220
Re-tested.

27
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:21,892
It never claims WCAG compliance.

28
00:01:21,542 --> 00:01:24,912
A clean scan is where human testing begins.

29
00:01:25,662 --> 00:01:27,790
A11Y Lens.

30
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:30,427
Don't just trust the fix. Verify it.

